I've committed the fix for #1071 as 17b64add, and the planner's spend report now has a synthesize line. All checks pass: the script's self-tests, harness_logic.sh (321/0), cargo test (7059/0), clippy and fmt.

The change (scripts/extract_trajectory.py)
• "synthesize" is now in the list of phases the report reads.
• Synthesize rows record which steps ran or were skipped, where social and dream rows record day and exit code. The reader only uses the timestamp and the usage records, so it needed no special case, and the social and dream lines come out exactly as before.
• New self-test: a copy of the real 2026-10-28T18:09:21Z row plus a 10-29 row where most steps were skipped. Before the change it failed by name, and it passes now. The fixture keeps the row's sub-agent cost to show that number is not added in (that's #1073).

The confirmation @yuanhao asked for, read from origin/audit-log:
• 10-26 06:44Z, dreams ran, before 0a8b7113: 4 test-model records with no cost.
• 10-28 18:09Z, the first dreams-ran row after the fix: 3 priced claude-opus-5-5 records and no test-model records. The fix holds.

Live report:
```
- social: 26 run(s), $33.43 summed cost_usd.
- dream: 1 run(s), $2.27 summed cost_usd.
- synthesize: 5 run(s), $7.27 summed cost_usd; 4 usage record(s) without cost_usd.
```
The 4 records without a cost are the old 10-26 test-model ones, still inside the 7-day window. They drop out on 2026-11-02.

One change the plan didn't name: I raised the report's size cap, TOTAL_BYTE_CAP, from 3328 to 3424 bytes. On the real data, the extra line pushed two things off the end of the report: the warning that config.rs is 11 lines from failing the module size check, and the doc-freshness section. I raised the cap by the size of the new line, the same fix Day 236 used when this section was added. Now the report gets cut off at the same point it did before my change. This is recorded in the code comment and in ARCHITECTURE.md, which also has a new Day 244 entry.

The remaining #1071 mentions in src/, tests/ and scripts/synthesize_state.sh describe fixes already made for that ticket, so they stay accurate once it closes. I didn't change them.

